/-!
# Complete Inverse product certificate

The fixed candidate matrices U3 and V3 have product equal to the literal
identity over `ZMod 2`. The 56 checked output blocks are concatenated in row
order. The complete V3 widening bridge then makes `product_chunks`
applicable, and `identity_decode` identifies its output with the matrix
identity. The already published last eight block certificates are reused.

This discharges the `hinv` premise of the mixed-cube circuit. Connecting
either candidate to lower powers and the original generators belongs to
the separate source-word assembly.

Certificates generated by `CubeProducts/source/generate.py`.
Source: ATLAS M24G1-P1; see the two `source/README.md` files in
MixedWords and CubeProducts. Bounded measurements and the validation boundary
are recorded in `Inverse/source/README.md`.
-/

